abstract: >-
  A prospectively registered fixed-geometry scalar-variance calibration at the
  exactly solvable minimal Euclidean/BD de Sitter reference. Independent forced
  modes, a finite-cutoff expression and matched time-memory formulas pass the
  registered comparisons, with explicit omitted-tail bounds and separate
  empirical numerical estimates. The archive preserves raw modes, state and
  contact controls, symbolic theory, analytic spectral-work distinctions and
  targeted primary-source provenance. No quantum stability, coupled evolution,
  heating or observational evidence is established. Reviews are internal and
  AI-assisted. The scalar response is a component rather than a complete
  stress/metric response. Text, figures and data use CC BY 4.0; code uses MIT.
